WEBVTT

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:18.160
Reality⨯VR

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.710
Hiro.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.010
I recall you wish to leave the city.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:37.980
Unfortunately, I can say with certainty
that you'll <i>never </i>leave alive.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.640
What do I do?

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.650
I can't even beat a normal goblin!
I'm no match for Tesla!

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.530
I'll let you in on another secret.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.700
I've been holding back this entire time.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:57.490
Lightning Extreme
has another, faster level:

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.410
Lightning Extreme Despair.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.170
I'll show it to you as a parting gift.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.710
Though, I suspect you won't see a thing!

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.260
No, duh!

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.930
I can't even follow the normal Lightning-
whatever! Like hell I could see this!

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.470
Kill him, Tesla.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.850
Take this!

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:21.060
Lightning Extreme Despair!

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.980
In the end I'm getting killed?!

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.030
I bet dying in this game hurts like hell!

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.240
And the game and my console break!

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.820
This is bullshit!

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:48.300
Alicia?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.890
So you defended your childhood friend...

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.890
A-Alicia protected me?

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.770
H-How can that be?

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.360
I mean...

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.110
Wh-Why?

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.570
Why would you save me?

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:15.240
You wanted to kill me!

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.490
My brother...

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.740
...spoke to me in a dream...

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.080
He said, "It's time to forgive Hiro.
He's not to blame."

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:31.090
I've been so awful to you, Hiro.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.510
So when I heard you'd joined the Guard,

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.510
I decided to join the
Guard, too, and protect you.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.430
Alicia, I...

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.190
Listen, Hiro.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.190
It made me so happy.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:52.570
When you said you wanted
to marry me one day,

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:57.200
I was truly happy.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.330
Alicia! Don't go!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:05.460
Don't die! Stay with me!

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:12.380
Hiro, live a full life,
for me and for Martin.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:27.270
Reona, do NPCs that die in
this game ever come back to life?

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.150
No.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.480
They don't.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.690
Of course.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.990
This shitty game pursues ultimate realism.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.530
Life would never be so convenient.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.040
Hey, Hiro. Done with your little funeral?

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.120
That wench died in vain.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:54.090
Her grand sacrifice only prolonged
your life by mere minutes!

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.800
Right. This is a game.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.970
Merely a home console full-dive RPG.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.760
And it was just an NPC that died.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.180
I know all that.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.930
Even so...

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.640
Even so...

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.570
You're at a dead end, Hiro!

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.230
Even so!

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:19.860
You piss me off even more than real life!

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.460
What?!

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:31.290
Was it a coincidence?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.000
But it won't happen again!

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:42.010
Lightning Extreme Despair!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.600
What?!

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.470
Impossible!

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.230
That was no coincidence!

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.390
He used his sword
to change the trajectory!

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.020
What's going on, Hiro? This is crazy!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.480
It's like right out of
a shonen manga plotline!

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.530
It's so bonkers that it's kinda creepy!

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.700
Don't say "creepy"!

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.700
Still, I'm surprised myself.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.330
To think that here, now,

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:11.040
against this opponent,
I'd activate Kamui's so-called trick.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.330
Now then, worm.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:19.300
The trick I'm about to
tell you ain't limited to KQ.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:24.390
As I'm sure you know,
the game faithfully recreates real life.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.510
In other words, though there
may be differences in degree,

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.440
this trick also exists in the real world.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:35.810
But just as you don't see
anybody at all using it in KQ,

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:39.900
you practically never see
anyone using it in real life.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.660
Seriously, the world is full of dumbasses.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:48.450
Ready? Listen up, worm
and world's biggest dumbass!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:53.170
The players stats in the game are
increased significantly by emotion.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:56.090
But not just any emotion!

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.590
The conviction not to give up!

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.590
A surging fire of feeling!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.180
Indomitable human will
pouring out from the soul!

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.890
It lets you exceed your limits,

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.930
and it even changes the course of destiny!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.020
<i>That </i>is the trick to KQ.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.440
No, I should say...

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.820
...that's reality itself.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.580
You trash!

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.670
Know your place!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.920
He dodged again?!

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:44.170
This amateur who doesn't even
know the basics of sword fighting?!

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.680
This can't be!

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.270
I can't see it...

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:56.350
I can't follow Hiro's movements at all.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:00.690
How can a human,
a player character, move like this?

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.030
It's just like...

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.160
...how Kamui moved!

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.830
All right!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.540
You got this, Hiro!

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.670
Kill that asshole!

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:19.920
Then let's get married!

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.760
Reona, though you're a total babe

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.970
and your boobs are huge,

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.600
I have little desire to marry you.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:47.910
What?

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.570
Huh?

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.000
The tables have turned, Hiro!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:05.420
I-It's true that it was rusty
and looked pretty old, but...

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.340
How shitty can this game be?!

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:13.180
I don't need this level of realism!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.520
It appears the heavens
have favored the great Tesla.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.310
Oh, crap!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.020
Die!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.020
Are you kidding?
After I had him cornered?!

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.280
N-No! Wait!

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.030
It's game over!

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:31.160
My console is toast!

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.670
The Kenura tree?

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.710
Martin?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.970
Hey, Hiro. It's been a while.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:52.640
Oh, so I really did die.

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:56.180
Yeah, it does feel
like a pretty long time.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.810
How are you doing?

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.640
Not great at all.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.230
Actually, I was killed by Tesla.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:05.360
And also, my console is about to be toast.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:11.820
And there's something else, Martin.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.620
Th-The truth is, Alicia...

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.120
...was also killed by Tesla.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.000
I see...

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.540
But I know you tried your hardest.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.800
Thanks, Martin.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.300
No need to thank me.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:34.010
Besides, Hiro, it's not over yet.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:34.930
Huh?

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.680
Would you take me with you this time?

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.020
Take you... with me?

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:44.440
Hey, now. You're the one
who said it to me, remember?

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.530
Oh, right. I did say that...

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.820
Let's go together.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.280
Let's fight together.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.240
Martin?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.290
I-Impossible!

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:16.260
What is that sword?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.980
My Gold Blade shattered?!

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:25.520
I see. Your sword is...

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.360
...magical!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.780
Bastard. You're a cursed blade wielder?

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.700
Magical?

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.450
For real?

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.200
Huh?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:45.460
"Sword Best Friend Killer User:
Amicidal Blade Wielder"?!

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.010
Did you hear that, Martin?

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:54.050
A cursed sword?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.720
That's ridiculous, huh.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:57.430
Besides...

00:10:57.430 --> 00:11:00.930
...you're the one who's cursed, Tesla!

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:05.770
It's a powerful weapon.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.400
But meaningless if you don't hit me.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.480
And that blade won't land a single blow.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.150
Behold!

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.780
A power greater than
Lightning Extreme Despair!

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:22.870
My ultimate technique:
Lightning Extreme Ultima!

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:25.960
Hiro, I'll gouge out your eye,

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:28.330
just like One-Eye.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:31.500
Hiro! He said, "ultimate technique"!
That sounds bad!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.130
Reona, don't worry.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.840
I'm not gonna lose.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.220
Hiro.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:44.020
It's not a tough guy act.
I actually feel certain I'll win.

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.430
"Ultimate" my ass.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.850
Ever since I killed Martin,

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.820
I've been pushed to
the ultimate edge of my limits!

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.570
Take this!

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:57.240
The ultimate speed!

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:01.240
Lightning Extreme Ultima!

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.250
I see him!

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:15.590
Well, turns out you lost.

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:18.680
I mean, I was surprised, too.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:21.470
To lose after all that.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.600
Who would've thought...

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.900
...that Govern would
come from behind like that?

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:39.410
Well, I didn't notice either,
so that's partly on me.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:43.200
But things got pretty gruesome
after that. With Tesla's torture.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.790
Definitely ZZ-rated.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.250
D-Don't bring that up!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:51.000
I don't wanna think about it.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.290
Right. Sorry.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:57.760
Things were also bad when
the game forcibly logged me out.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:04.560
The game and the
console were literally smoking.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.480
So when are you gonna try again?

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.690
Huh?

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.020
I know.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:16.360
You don't have the money to
rebuy the game and a console.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.240
Not a problem!

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:22.410
Because of the promise I see in you,
I'll rent them to you for free!

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:25.780
A special freebie for my future husband!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.620
Listen, about that...

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.750
I need to give it some thought.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:34.920
What? You're kidding!
Are you planning to quit?

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.170
Hmm...

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:41.800
Hiro! I haven't seen anyone get so close
to beating the beginning in years!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:43.130
<u>Idiots who want One-Eye in their party</u>

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:43.130
<u>Trash who let the goblin kids die</u>

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.640
Have some confidence!

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.600
Yeah...

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.180
Fools

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.180
Fools

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.930
When I got the Amicide
title in the beginning,

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:53.270
I actually wanted to start over.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:50.180
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:50.220
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:50.260
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:50.300
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:50.350
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:50.390
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:50.430
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:50.470
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:50.510
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:50.550
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:50.600
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:50.720
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:50.760
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.430
{=0}Best Friend Killer: Amicide

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.520
But now,

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.480
imagining everything
I went through being erased...

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.320
it's oddly demotivating.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.360
m 982 178 l 964 278 962 286 892 362 853 413 838 442 837 469 857 524 891 590 219 603 217 42 1059 59 1013 92

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.360
<u>Fools who, after the goblin assault,
were ultimately defeated at the last moment
and ruined their consoles
but still can't quite call it quits</u>

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.160
Huh?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:09.160
Hold on a moment, Reona.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.960
Why? You need to potty?

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:17.250
This entry wasn't here before.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:22.380
Was it only displayed after
Kamui revealed the trick?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.930
What did I tell ya?
You lost, didn't you, worm?

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:30.770
I warned you it was a 0.1% chance.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:32.940
This guy still pisses me off!

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:34.140
What's the deal?

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:38.110
After getting killed and losing your
console, you still wanna play KQ?

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.400
Are you a real masochist or something?

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.400
How creepy. Super freaking creepy.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:44.860
Sh-Shut up!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.280
I said I need time to think about it!

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:52.040
I'll let you in on a little secret, creep.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:57.710
With this secret technique,
you can restart from before you died!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.630
Secret technique?!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:03.470
For a realistic game, there sure are
a lot of tricks and secret techniques.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:06.260
To do it, you have to
boot up a new console,

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:10.760
insert the broken game,
and finish this within ten seconds.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.100
Listen up.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:20.860
"Yuute emiya uokemu kougo riiyo ujitori
mayaa giira pepepepe pepepe pepepe pe"

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:24.280
Shout that loudly.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.240
Huh?

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.620
Afterwards, immediately
switch to a fresh game cartridge.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:33.910
If it goes well, you can resume play
from about an hour before you died.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:40.340
But even with a redo, a worm like you
would probably just end up dying agai--

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.760
I-I can do it!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.550
I can do it from where I was!

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.560
Wh-What's going on, Hiro?

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:54.100
You just keep saying
"do it" and it's creepy!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:57.810
Getting to start one hour
before my death means...

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:02.230
...if I do things right
I can save Alicia this time!

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.400
All right! I'm raring to go now!

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.950
Wh-What's gotten into you, Hiro?

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:11.080
It's possible to continue
from previous save data

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:16.950
Game Shop Kisaragi

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:13.490
if you shout, "yuute emiya
uokemu kougo riiyo ujitori mayaa

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:18.330
giira pepepepe pepepe pe!"

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.500
Hiro, have you lost it?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.590
You're scaring me right now.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.170
I'm completely sane!

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.800
Kamui told me this on his website!

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:31.010
Really? Assuming you can restart,

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.470
what if you fight Tesla again and lose?

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:40.270
I basically remember how
it felt to activate the trick.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:45.110
But I can't say for certain
my chances of beating Tesla are high.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.820
Reona.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:51.870
One month.

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:53.910
Give me one month.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:57.910
There's something I'd like
to do before we restart.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:13.550
Why am I doing all this for a game?

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:16.310
This feeling...

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:20.350
I'd forgotten how much
I loved just running.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.270
I'm back.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:30.700
I'm amazed you can do
that right before school starts.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:33.410
The morning air feels better.

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:39.370
Well, running suits you much better
than holing up in your room playing games.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.000
Oh, I see.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:45.170
I-I just meant that, compared
to playing a dead full-dive RPG,

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.050
it's just <i>slightly </i>better.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:49.840
Don't call it dead.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.510
You're right.

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:55.390
It's way past being
a dead game at this point.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:59.980
It's completely faded and erased from
society's memory. Utterly forgotten.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:03.150
It hasn't faded and
it's not forgotten either!

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:07.610
How much fun do you need to
make of full-dive RPGs, anyway?

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:09.900
Oh, I forgot. One more thing.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.700
You're still not done?

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:15.410
Apparently running with a towel
around your neck leads to heatstroke,

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:17.490
so be careful.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.580
I really don't get her.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.130
Man...

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.750
m 568 394 l 570 475 288 392 278 322

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.750
Faculty Room

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.130
You still haven't decided?

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:34.050
Like I said last time, you really need to
at least choose between college and work--

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.430
Don't worry.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:41.270
I'm giving deliberate thought to it,
so I'll have an answer soon. Promise.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:45.560
Yuki, your expression
seems different from before.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.270
Could it be that

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.940
you also read this book?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.020
Turning Pain Into Strength

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.020
Post-Graduation Plans

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:53.780
That's so funny!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:57.990
Hey, come on now.
I'm giving serious answers here.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:02.500
You know, Hiro,
you've really changed somehow.

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:06.040
Well, I've been running in the morning,
and I think I've narrowed it down.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:10.050
No, I mean it's not just your body.
Your expression, too.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:12.460
Oh, really?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:13.840
Hiro!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:19.180
A classmate was saying recently you've
been running and working out and stuff.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:21.140
Y-Yeah.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:22.600
Hey, Hiro...

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:27.480
This working out stuff.
It wouldn't be that maybe, just maybe,

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:30.940
it's so you can knock us flat, is it?

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.530
Huh? No, I...

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.320
Then how come you're doing it?

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:39.490
W-Well...

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.420
I win.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:58.550
Now, it's time for a cocky
brat to get his punishment.

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:04.600
That damned bastard!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:07.230
Next time I'll freakin' kill him!

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:10.020
I wanna actually gouge his eyes out!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.020
H-Hiro?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.990
Wh-Who do you mean?

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:18.860
D-Don't ya think eye gouging
is a little overboard?

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:25.830
Oh! N-No, no. That was
about a video game! Um...

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.410
See ya...

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.080
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:33.380
Oh, shit. The guy snapped!

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.170
Now I've done it.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.300
They'll definitely think I'm crazy.

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:42.100
W-Well, maybe it's for the best.
They had it coming.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:56.490
She's just as unpunctual as she looks.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.780
I shouldn't have rushed over here.

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:20.840
Martin?

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:23.470
What's up, worm?

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:31.150
You know, I've been meaning to say,
who're you calling a worm?

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.560
Huh?

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:37.440
This version of you is about my age,
right? What's your problem?

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.740
What's wrong with calling a worm a worm?

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:43.990
You got killed by Tesla and
had your console fried, right?

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.910
Worm totally fits.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:51.080
Yeah, you're right. I did.
But I'm about to restart

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.500
with the method you taught me.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:57.090
You're still gonna play?
You don't know when to give up.

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:59.260
About that though, Kamui.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:04.970
The fact that you know that
method of restoring the game...

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:08.930
You actually had your
console fried, too, didn't you?

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:15.060
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:24.950
Hiro. Come with me.

00:22:24.950 --> 00:22:29.040
I'll teach you all about real life.

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:30.410
Sure.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:33.540
That arrogance again--

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:36.960
Hiro, are you awake?

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:39.130
Oh, uh, yeah...

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.300
I guess I fell asleep.

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:43.970
Wait, did you just do something to me?

00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:48.180
It kinda felt like
something soft hit me...

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:51.930
You were sleeping so cutely, so...

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:53.440
I gave you a little

00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:56.690
booboop.

00:22:56.690 --> 00:22:58.730
Hey, what's a "booboop"?

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:00.730
What exactly did you do to me?

00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:02.070
It's a secret.

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:03.990
Really, what did you do?

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:07.240
I'm super curious to know!

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:10.330
More importantly, Hiro,

00:23:10.330 --> 00:23:12.910
are you ready?

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:16.290
Y-Yeah. I should be.

00:23:20.090 --> 00:23:23.260
I've gained strength.

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:26.970
I even did fight simulations.

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:30.310
Of course I'm prepared.

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:32.890
So now,

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:35.850
it's time to go back!

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:41.530
To the world of that shitty game
that's realer than real life!
